    <statement><p>Consider the sequence <m>10, 15, 20, 25, \ldots, 5n + 0\text{.}</m></p>
<p><ol label="a.">
<li>
<p>How many terms are there in the sequence?  Your answer will be in terms of <m>n\text{.}</m></p>
<p><fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p>What is the second-to-last term?</p>
<p><fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Find the sum of all the terms in the sequence, in terms of <m>n\text{.}</m></p>
<p><fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>n-2+1</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>5n+\left(-5\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{\left(5n+10\right)\mathopen{}\left(n-2+1\right)}{2}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p><ol label="a.">
<li>
<p><m>{n-2+1}</m> terms, since to get <m>10</m> using the formula <m>5n+0</m> we must use <m>n=2\text{.}</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>5n - 5\text{,}</m> which is 5 less than <m>5n+0</m> (or plug in <m>n-1</m> for <m>n</m>).</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\frac{(5n+10)*({n-2+1})}{2}\text{.}</m>  Reverse and add.  Each sum gives the constant <m>5n+10</m>, and there are <m>{n-2+1}</m> terms.</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</solution>
